QModem pages: space between buttons, and between a log and its buttons

The Dial Overview and modem debug pages build their buttons in script and append them one
after another, with no whitespace between them, and put some of them straight under a
textarea. Nothing in the markup separates them, so under any theme the buttons touched each
other and the log box above them: the Modem Log's Download and Clear, the AT console's
Clear, the debug page's paired Submit buttons.

Each page's own stylesheet now gives a button that follows another button 8px, and a button
row under a textarea 12px. Rows the theme already lays out with a gap (.right) are left
alone, so they do not get the space twice.

Dial Overview also appends its Modem Status and Modem Log cards after the page's form, right
behind the Reset / Save / Save & Apply bar. Vantage floats that bar with space above it only,
so the Modem Status card touched it; the card now keeps 16px from it.

Advance Modem Settings appended its Submit, Select All and Scan buttons straight into a
<tbody> or <table>. That is not table content: the browser hoists each button into an
anonymous cell, and under Vantage they sat on top of the band rows (Lock Band) or against the
card edge (Dial Mode, Neighbor Cell). They now sit in a real row (createBtnRow), with 8px
between them. Its radios and checkboxes had their labels glued to them and to the next
choice ("qmigobinet", "3G4G5G"); each label now keeps 6px from its box and 16px from the
next choice, and the band list keeps 8px between bands.

Applies to: https://github.com/FUjr/QModem.git @ 0988085b, after 0010.
Upstream status: local to CleanWRT.

